@startuml diag-topo-part2

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false

title Topologie réseau --- Partie 2 : VLAN 10 (Zone IoT) et VLAN 20 (Zone DMZ)\nFlux MQTT/TLS et inspection IDS passive

node "MikroTik CHR v7\n192.168.1.2" as MIKROTIK #D1C4E9

package "VLAN 10 — Zone IoT Devices\n192.168.10.0/24 — GW : 192.168.10.1" #E8F5E9 {
  node "fleet-simulator\n192.168.10.100\nPython 3.11 / paho-mqtt\n50 threads concurrents" as FLEET
  node "device-001 … device-050\n192.168.10.11 … .60\nCertificats X.509 individuels\nPublie toutes les 5 s (QoS 1)" as DEVS
}

package "VLAN 20 — Zone DMZ Services\n192.168.20.0/24 — GW : 192.168.20.1" #FFF9C4 {
  node "Mosquitto v2.0\n192.168.20.10\nPort 8883 (MQTT/TLS 1.3 + mTLS)\nACL deny-by-default" as MOSQ
  node "Suricata v7.0\n192.168.20.20\nMode AF_PACKET (passif)\nParseur MQTT natif" as SUR
}

interface "MQTT over TLS 1.3\nPort 8883" as IMQTT
interface "Port miroir\n(copie trafic VLAN 20)" as ISPAN

MIKROTIK -down-> FLEET 
MIKROTIK -down-> DEVS  : VLAN 10
MIKROTIK -down-> MOSQ  : VLAN 20
MIKROTIK -down-> ISPAN : Port miroir eth1.20

FLEET --> IMQTT
DEVS  --> IMQTT
IMQTT --> MOSQ

ISPAN --> SUR : Inspection\npassive (AF_PACKET)

note bottom of MOSQ
  ACL Mosquitto :
  iot/+/telemetry → pub (devices)
  iot/+/telemetry → sub (admin)
  iot/+/cmd       → sub (devices)
  Tout autre topic : DENY
end note

note bottom of SUR
  Règles Suricata actives :
  alert mqtt brute-force
  alert mqtt flood > 100/s
  alert tls cert expired
  Sortie : EVE JSON → Wazuh
end note

@enduml
